weewx-wh23xx
Copyright 2016 Matthew Wall
License: GPLv3

This is a weewx driver for Fine Offset WH23xx hardware.  These stations are
commonly available as Tycon TP2700 and Froggit WH4000 weather stations.

Installation

0) install weewx, select 'Simulator' driver

http://weewx.com/docs/usersguide.htm#installing

1) download the driver

wget -O weewx-wh23xx.zip https://github.com/matthewwall/weewx-wh23xx/archive/master.zip

2) install the driver

sudo wee_extension --install weewx-wh23xx.zip

3) configure the driver

sudo wee_config --reconfigure

4) start weewx

sudo /etc/init.d/weewx start

Independent continuation (0.15.0)

This repository preserves matthewwall/weewx-wh23xx history and GPL-3.0-only
licensing. Python 3 fixes build on upstream PR #12. PR #11's exception syntax
was not used: `except (IndexError, e)` does not bind the exception to e.

    weectl extension install https://github.com/weewx-packages/weewx-wh23xx/archive/refs/tags/v0.15.0.zip
    weectl station reconfigure --driver=user.wh23xx --config=/path/to/weewx.conf

The configurator supports --info, --info-all, --current, --sync-time,
--eeprom-time, --eeprom-dump-raw and --clear-history through `weectl device`.
Stop WeeWX before accessing the USB device. Mutating operations prompt first.

The driver accepts vendor_id and product_id in [WH23xx], for example
`vendor_id = 0x10c4` and `product_id = 0x8468`. Different IDs alone do not prove
protocol compatibility. Confirm the device and a valid checksum before use.

Run `python -m pytest -q tests`. Tests exercise split USB records, checksum
rejection, bounded retries, Python 3 decoding, configurator access, and WeeWX
editor loading. Verify WH2303/WH2310/WH2315 operation on the actual devices.
